<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The AURIX mark, as a notification small icon.

    ## Why this file exists

    `audio_service` defaults `androidNotificationIcon` to `mipmap/ic_launcher`,
    and AURIX was taking that default. Android does not draw a small icon: it
    takes the icon's *alpha channel* as a stencil and fills it with the system
    tint. A launcher icon is a fully opaque square, so its stencil is a square —
    which is why an app that ships its launcher icon here shows a solid white
    block in the status bar and in the notification's header instead of a mark.

    So this is the AURIX "A" as white-on-transparent geometry, which is what the
    stencil needs. `AudioServiceConfig.androidNotificationIcon` points at it by
    resource name (`drawable/ic_stat_aurix`) — see `initAudioService`.

    ## Why the proportions are not exactly the launcher's

    The letterform is the same two-legged apex plus a detached crossbar as
    `AurixLogo` and `generate_launcher_icons.dart`, but drawn at a heavier
    relative stroke and with the crossbar's clearance opened up. At the brand's
    own weight the gap between the crossbar and the legs is under 4% of the
    mark's width, which is a crisp detail at 96dp on the profile header and a
    smudge at the 18px a status bar actually renders. The alternative — using
    the exact geometry and letting it fill in — is a mark that reads as a solid
    triangle, and a triangle is not the AURIX "A".

    24dp canvas with the mark inside the middle 20dp, per Android's small-icon
    guidance. The colour here is ignored at runtime; only the alpha is read.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">

    <!-- The two legs meeting at a rounded apex. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M6,18.5 L12,5.5 L18,18.5"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.9"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"/>

    <!-- The detached crossbar. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M10.2,15.25 L13.8,15.25"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="1.9"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"/>
</vector>
